In (and after) compiling NetHack on the Macintosh I noticed a couple
of problems that should probably be mentioned.

1> The 'Install.Mac' document should probably be rewritten as many
items are unclear, possibly inaccurate and, in some cases, never
mentioned in the document.  I sometimes think that these kinds of
documents should be written for an idiot (knowing some of those
sys-ops out there at least :-)  (flames welcome, you don't have my
address, and I can always press 'n' :-) ))

2> The mac code seems to be quite buggy still (I don't really think
that the problem (as explained below) is in the rest of the code, but
it could be...) as it never seems to make up it's mind as to whether
or not the user should actually play the game.  I've had problems
with the code working fine for a couple of games and suddenly bus
(or address) errors pop up next time I start the game.

3> Something strange (again probably in the mac code) is happening
during game execution.  After exiting the game, I've had problems with
the Finder blowing up.  Perhaps a dangling pointer somewhere?

4> There isn't a way to get the stronghold option to work.  Also the
patch expects certain external variables to be declared if SMALLDATA
is defined, these variables are NOT defined if STRONGHOLD is not
defined.

5> Some sort of 'config' file should be allowed to exist.  Starting
up, I'm getting sick of being asked to locate the save file for a
character and want to be able to turn that off.

6> The program doesn't seem to be able to find all it's data files,
explicitly 'rumors'.  The file exists in the directory with NetHack,
but the program can never open the file for reading a fortune.

7> The Finder Icons (and Fonts for that matter) need to be changed,
the originals are rather ugly.  I've 'beutified' the icons and text,
and if anyone is interested (hint, hint, Magic Co.) I'm quite willing
to provide these better looking fonts for all.

8> There are problems with Multifinder switching.  Seems that for some
reasons (rather sporatic) all the menus except for Apple, File and
Edit disappear.  Not good.

9> The resources should possibly be packed as 'ResEdit' files, since
you have the nethack font packed, why not everything else too?  Some
of us NEVER use the resource compilers, and just as soon wouldn't want
to.  As is, I had to go and change several resources that wern't
written properly for RMaker (specifically the Menu resource, you need
an extra / in there guys).

10> Make an option to turn off the blinking cursor (pun intended) I
HATE the thing and would like to see a plain cursor there.  See the
section on the config (option) file above.

11> Nice game otherwise, great job guys!


